# Store and check out LF everywhere, on every platform.
#
# Deliberately not "* text=auto": that lets git guess per platform, so a Windows
# checkout turns every file into CRLF while the agent edits them back to LF, and the
# working tree ends up full of changes that are not changes. Java, Gradle and JSON do
# not care which one is used, so pin it and remove the ambiguity.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Structure templates are gzipped NBT. They must never go through any line-ending
# conversion - a single flipped byte makes the template unreadable, and the failure
# would surface as "the machine silently never forms".
*.nbt binary
*.jar binary
*.png binary
